  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "A massive whirlpool swallowed eleven barges and an oil rig. In 1980, Louisiana's shallow Lake Peigneur suddenly began draining like an unplugged bathtub.",
        "visual_query": "louisiana lake bayou water aerial",
        "visual_fallback": "swamp lake aerial"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The vortex grew into a quarter-mile-wide abyss. Trees, loading docks, and sixty-five acres of surrounding land were sucked straight downward.",
        "visual_query": "massive whirlpool swirling water vortex",
        "visual_fallback": "rushing water vortex"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Even crazier? The canal connected to the Gulf of Mexico reversed direction, creating a roaring 150-foot waterfall.",
        "visual_query": "rushing river waterfall muddy canyon",
        "visual_fallback": "turbulent waterfall river"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The culprit was a single miscalculated drill bit from an oil rig that accidentally pierced the roof of an active salt mine underneath.",
        "visual_query": "deep underground salt mine cavern",
        "visual_fallback": "underground mine tunnel"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Rushing water dissolved the salt pillars and gutted the mine, yet perfectly timed evacuation plans meant every single worker survived.",
        "visual_query": "flooded underground cavern dark mine",
        "visual_fallback": "dark cave water"
      }
    ],
